   "id": "5c4a7f56",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "import matplotlib.pyplot as plt\n",
    "import pandas as pd\n",
    "import numpy as np\n",
    "import seaborn as sns\n",
    "\n",
    "url = \"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/datasciencedojo/datasets/master/titanic.csv\"\n",
    "\n",
    "df = pd.read_csv(url)"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "273ac1ef",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 1 — Histogram with insight\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "51d91ae1",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Plot the distribution of Fare. Add mean and median lines. Write a one-sentence insight as the chart title describing what you see about the distribution shape."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 3,
   "id": "5073847a",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1000x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig , ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(10,5))\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.hist(df[\"Fare\"].dropna(),\n",
    "        bins=30,\n",
    "        color=\"#5C6BC0\",\n",
    "        edgecolor=\"white\",\n",
    "        linewidth=0.5\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.axvline(df[\"Fare\"].mean(), color=\"#E53935\", linewidth=2,\n",
    "           linestyle=\"--\", label=f\"Mean: {df['Fare'].mean():.1f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.axvline(df[\"Fare\"].median(), color=\"#43A047\", linewidth=2,\n",
    "           linestyle=\"--\", label=f\"Median: {df['Fare'].median():.1f}\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Fare distribution is strongly right-skewed, with most passengers paying lower fares and a few paying very high fares.\",\n",
    "             fontsize=14, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Fare\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"No Of Passengers\")\n",
    "ax.legend()\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "493ed0a8",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 2 — Bar chart\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "b4d803ae",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Show the survival rate (as a percentage) for each embarkation port. Color the bars meaningfully. Write an insight title."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 8,
   "id": "762717ee",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x400 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "survival_by_embarked = df.groupby(\"Embarked\")[\"Survived\"].mean()*100\n",
    "\n",
    "fig , ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8,4))\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.bar([\"S\",\"C\",\"Q\"],\n",
    "       survival_by_embarked.values,\n",
    "       color=[\"#43A047\", \"#FDD835\", \"#E53935\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Embarkation Port\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Survival Rate (%)\")\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Passengers from S had the highest survival rate\",\n",
    "             fontsize=14, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "2252e10c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Task 3 — Boxplot\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "60ec0f7b",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Compare the fare distribution between survivors and non-survivors using a boxplot. What does the difference tell you?"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 12,
   "id": "8866b525",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x500 with 1 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig , ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8,5))\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.boxplot(data=df, x=\"Survived\", y=\"Fare\", ax=ax)\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Survival: 0 = No & 1 = Yes\")\n",
    "ax.set_ylabel(\"Fare\")\n",
    "ax.set_xlabel(\"Survival\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "62a57490",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 4 — Heatmap\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "7be05171",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Create a correlation heatmap for all numeric columns. Identify the two strongest correlations with Survived. Write your findings as a markdown cell below the chart.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "id": "868dd030",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 800x500 with 2 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "numeric_col = df.select_dtypes(include=\"number\").columns\n",
    "corr = df[numeric_col].corr()\n",
    "\n",
    "fig ,ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8,5))\n",
    "\n",
    "sns.heatmap(corr,\n",
    "            annot=True,\n",
    "            fmt=\".2f\",\n",
    "            cmap=\"coolwarm\",\n",
    "            center=0,\n",
    "            square=True,\n",
    "            linewidth=0.5,\n",
    "            ax=ax)\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "ax.set_title(\"Correlation Heatmap of Numeric Variables\",\n",
    "             fontsize=14, fontweight=\"bold\")\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "490bafbb",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### Findings\n",
    "The two strongest correlations with Survived are Pclass (negative correlation) and Fare (positive correlation)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "72fc1f02",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Task 5 — Subplots\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "id": "e1d28f6c",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "Create a 2×2 subplot figure answering these four questions:\n",
    "\n",
    "How many passengers in each class?\n",
    "What is the survival rate by sex?\n",
    "How does age differ between survivors and non-survivors?\n",
    "What is the fare distribution by embarkation port?\n",
    "\n",
    "Give the whole figure a title. Each subplot should have its own insight title.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": 28,
   "id": "f8704af1",
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [
    {
     "data": {
      "image/png": "",
      "text/plain": [
       "<Figure size 1400x1000 with 4 Axes>"
      ]
     },
     "metadata": {},
     "output_type": "display_data"
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "fig, axes = plt.subplots(2, 2, figsize=(14, 10))\n",
    "\n",
    "fig.suptitle(\n",
    "    \"Titanic Survival Analysis — Key Factors\",\n",
    "    fontsize=16,\n",
    "    fontweight=\"bold\",\n",
    "    y=1.01\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "# Chart 1 — Passengers in each Class\n",
    "sns.countplot(data=df, x=\"Pclass\", ax=axes[0, 0])\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_title(\"Third Class Has the Most Passengers\")\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_xlabel(\"Passenger Class\")\n",
    "axes[0, 0].set_ylabel(\"Number of Passengers\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Chart 2 — Survival by Sex\n",
    "sns.countplot(\n",
    "    data=df,\n",
    "    x=\"Sex\",\n",
    "    hue=\"Survived\",\n",
    "    ax=axes[0, 1]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_title(\"Females Had a Higher Survival Rate\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_xlabel(\"Sex\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].set_ylabel(\"Number of Passengers\")\n",
    "axes[0, 1].legend([\"Died\", \"Survived\"])\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Chart 3 — Age Distribution by Survival\n",
    "sns.histplot(\n",
    "    data=df,\n",
    "    x=\"Age\",\n",
    "    hue=\"Survived\",\n",
    "    bins=25,\n",
    "    kde=True,\n",
    "    ax=axes[1, 0]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_title(\"Age Distribution by Survival\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_xlabel(\"Age\")\n",
    "axes[1, 0].set_ylabel(\"Number of Passengers\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "# Chart 4 — Fare Distribution by Embarkation\n",
    "sns.boxplot(\n",
    "    data=df,\n",
    "    x=\"Embarked\",\n",
    "    y=\"Fare\",\n",
    "    ax=axes[1, 1]\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_title(\"Fare Distribution by Embarkation Port\")\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_xlabel(\"Embarkation Port\")\n",
    "axes[1, 1].set_ylabel(\"Fare\")\n",
    "\n",
    "\n",
    "plt.tight_layout()\n",
    "plt.show()"
   ]
  },
